## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross-topic correlation with late data, per-key state, and exactly-once guarantees, plus practical testing and recovery considerations.

## Key Concepts
- Windowing and watermarking for cross-topic joins
- Per-user bounded state store
- Idempotent emission and deduplication across partitions
- Backpressure handling and rebalance safety

## Code Example
```java
// Pseudocode
Map<String, ClickInfo> lastClick = new HashMap<>();
void onClick(Click c) { lastClick.put(c.userId, new ClickInfo(c.clickTs, c.item)); }
void onPurchase(Purchase p) {
  ClickInfo c = lastClick.get(p.userId);
  if (c != null && p.purchaseTs - c.clickTs <= 5*60*1000) {
    emit(new CompositeEvent(p.userId, c.clickTs, p.purchaseTs, c.item, p.amount), p.userId + p.purchaseTs);
  }
}
```

